blocks.en:
Finding 2 Strong models write hints for students like themselves;
for weaker students the same hints are too complex to carry out,
and they turn correct attempts into wrong ones.

blocks.zh:
发现2个强力模型为自己这样的学生写出提示;
对弱小的学生来说 同样的暗示太复杂了 无法执行
他们把正确的尝试变成错误的尝试。

blocks.en:
Figure 3: The best teacher is not the best solver. Left: attempts each author’s hint fixes (orange) and breaks (purple);
a mid-ranked solver writes the most useful hints. Right: the breaks come from strong authors’ hints reaching weak solvers,
while strong solvers are almost never harmed.

blocks.zh:
图3:最优秀的老师不是最优秀的解题师. 左:尝试每个作者的提示修正(橙色)和中断(纯色);
一个排名中位的解析器会写出最有用的提示. 对:这些突破来自作者向弱解者的暗示,
强力的解答者几乎永远不会受到伤害。
